#lang saffron
;; saffron-lang-plan S6: the Saffron prelude, auto-loaded for a `#lang saffron`
;; ENTRY file.
;;
;; ADAPTORS, NOT REIMPLEMENTATIONS (R5).  `vec-map`/`vec-filter`/`vec-fold`
;; forward to the typed stdlib and exist only because the typed signature is
;; unreachable from dynamic code: a `(Vec any)` cannot be handed to a
;; `[A B] [v (Vec A) f (fn [A] B)]` without naming A and B, which is the whole
;; thing Saffron removes.
;;
;; The prelude is scoped to the ENTRY file: a Saffron file IMPORTED by a
;; Turmeric program does not drag it in, and a Turmeric file checked in the same
;; process right after a Saffron one does not see it either (the flag is set on
;; every dialect detection, true or false, rather than only when true).
;;
;; The prelude itself is `#lang saffron` -- a DIRECTIVE in the file rather than
;; a filename special-case in the two loaders -- because its own bodies use D4
;; truthiness (`(when (pred x) ...)` where `pred` returns `any`), which is a hard
;; "if condition must be bool, got any" under Turmeric.  The interpreter's
;; `(load ...)` already ran `#lang` detection; the compiled autoload path learned
;; to, so the file says what it is instead of two call sites remembering.
;;
;; Writing it is what found the fourth and fifth `any`-carrier straddles (a
;; `let` binding and a fat-closure `any` slot) -- see
;; docs/reported/any-carrier-straddle-is-bridged-per-consumer.md.
;;
;; requires.leak-check.  Each of these returns a fresh vector the caller owns,
;; and every INPUT vector is bound and freed too -- which is the point of
;; writing it this way rather than passing the literals inline.
;;
;; `(vec-map [1 2 3] f)` leaks the `[1 2 3]`: a `[...]` literal in argument
;; position is never bound, so `vec-free` has nothing to name.  That is explicit
;; memory management working as designed, not a defect -- Turmeric frees a
;; vector when the author says so -- but it is a sharp edge a dynamic dialect
;; makes very easy to hit, and a fixture that demonstrated the prelude by
;; leaking on every line would be the wrong example to copy.

(defn main []
  (let [src [1 2 3]]
    (let [doubled (vec-map src (fn [x] (* x 2)))]
      (println (vec-len doubled))
      (println (vec-get doubled 0))
      (println (vec-get doubled 2))
      (vec-free doubled))
    (vec-free src))
  (let [src4 [1 2 3 4]]
    (let [big (vec-filter src4 (fn [x] (> x 2)))]
      (println (vec-len big))
      (println (vec-get big 0))
      (vec-free big))
    (vec-free src4))
  (let [si [1 2 3]]
    (println (vec-fold si 0 (fn [a x] (+ a x))))
    (vec-free si))
  (let [sf [1.5 2.25]]
    (println (vec-fold sf 0.0 (fn [a x] (+ a x))))
    (vec-free sf))
  0)
